translated_text:
Part Tenth

Facilitation of Juvenile Criminal Justice

Article 77

(1) The Regional Government has a role in facilitating the juvenile criminal justice process based on the principle of restorative justice. JDIH Kota Singkawang

(2) Facilitation of the juvenile criminal justice process as referred to in paragraph (1) includes: a. capacity building of human resources whose tasks are related to juvenile criminal justice and the community;

b. increased coordination with law enforcement officials; c. development of effective methods through information support, facilities and positive activities as well as taking immediate action on gaps that encourage children and/or groups of children to commit legal violations;

d. provision and delivery of legal and psychosocial assistance services in realizing restorative justice and diversion processes for children in conflict with the law;

e. encouraging a paradigm shift in society towards children in conflict with the law;

f. developing diversion mechanisms for children in conflict with the law in accordance with Laws and Regulations; g. developing cooperation with relevant agencies or institutions in organizing education, guidance and counseling programs for handling children who commit criminal acts, especially children under 12 (twelve) years of age to achieve optimal development; and

h. provision of facilities and infrastructure supporting the juvenile justice process by prioritizing the best interests of the child in accordance with the provisions of Laws and Regulations.

(3) Further provisions regarding the facilitation of juvenile criminal justice as referred to in paragraph (1), and paragraph (2) shall be regulated by Mayor's Regulation.

