translated_text:
Article 98

Every person is prohibited from:

a. receiving child visitors and employing children in discotheque businesses, nightclubs, bars, karaoke, pubs/music houses, massage parlors and steam baths/saunas, and/or other worst places of work for children.
b. producing, selling and/or promoting cigarettes in the school environment.
c. selling and/or promoting cigarettes, gambling equipment, contraceptives and goods that can damage the morals of children.
d. broadcasting and displaying pornographic acts in community activities that can be accessed by children.
e. receiving child visitors during school hours or allowing child visitors after nine o'clock at night to access the internet at internet cafes.
f. refusing complaints and/or collecting fees in providing services to victims at Protection Service Institutions. g. treating children discriminatorily resulting in children experiencing material and moral losses thereby hindering their social function; h. treating children with disabilities discriminatorily; i. placing, allowing, involving, ordering the involvement of children in situations of mistreatment and neglect;
J. placing, allowing, committing, ordering to commit or participating in committing violence against children;
k. committing violence or threat of violence forcing a child to have sexual intercourse with him/her or with another person; I. committing violence or threat of violence, coercing, committing fraud, committing a series of lies, or persuading a child to commit or allow indecent acts to be committed; m. placing, allowing, committing, ordering to commit or participating in committing kidnapping, sale, and/or trafficking of children;

JDIH Kota Singkawang n. obstructing children from enjoying their own culture, recognizing and implementing the teachings of their religion and/or using their own language without neglecting access to community and cultural development;

o. recruiting or exploiting children for military and/or other purposes, and leaving children without protection of life;

| p. placing, allowing, committing, ordering to commit, or | participating in committing economic and/or sexual exploitation | against children; |
|---|---|---|
| q. intentionally placing, allowing, involving, ordering | the involvement of children in the abuse, as well as production and distribution | of narcotics and/or psychotropic substances; and |
| r. intentionally placing, allowing, involving, ordering | the involvement of children in the abuse, as well as production and distribution | of alcohol and other addictive substances. |

text:
Pasal 99

( 1) Pejabat Pegawai Negeri Sipil tertentu di lingkungan Pemerintah Daerah diberi wewenang khusus sebagai penyidik untuk melakukan penyidikan terhadap perbuatan pidana yang diatur dalam Peraturan Daerah ini sebagaimana dimaksud dalam Kitab Undang-Undang Hukum Acara Pidana.

(2) Wewenang penyidikan sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1), adalah sebagai berikut: a . menerima, mencari, mengumpulkan, dan meneliti keterangan atau laporan berkenaan dengan tindak pidana perlindungan anak dan perempuan agar keterangan atau laporan tersebut menjadi lebih lengkap dan jelas;

b. meneliti, mencari, dan mengumpulkan keterangan mengenai orang pribadi atau badan tentang kebenaran perbuatan yang dilakukan sehubungan dengan tindak pidana perlindungan anak dan perempuan; c . meminta keterangan dan bahan bukti dari orang pribadi atau badan sehubungan dengan tindak pidana perlindungan anak dan perempuan;

d. memeriksa buku, catatan, dan dokumen lain berkenaan dengan tindak pidana Perlindungan anak dan perempuan;

JDIH Kota Singkawang

e. melakukan penggeledahan untuk mendapatkan bahan bukti pembukuan, pencatatan, dan dokumen lain, serta melakukan penyitaan terhadap bahan bukti tersebut;

f. meminta bantuan tenaga ahli dalam rangka pelaksanaan tugas penyidikan tindak pidana perlindungan anak dan perempuan; g. menyuruh berhenti dan/atau melarang seseorang meninggalkan ruangan atau tempat pada saat pemeriksaan sedang berlangsung dan memeriksa identitas orang, benda, dan/atau dokumen yang dibawa; h . memotret seseorang yang berkaitan dengan tindak pidana perlindungan anak dan perempuan;

i. memanggil orang untuk didengar keterangannya dan diperiksa sebagai tersangka atau saksi;

J. menghentikan penyidikan; dan/atau

k. melakukan tindakan lain yang perlu untuk kelancaran penyidikan tindak pidana perlindungan anak dan perempuan sesuai dengan ketentuan Peraturan Perundang-undangan.

(3) Dalam hal penyidikan memenuhi unsur sebagaimana dimaksud pada ayat (1) Penyidik memberitahukan dimulainya penyidikan dan menyampaikan hasil penyidikannya kepada Penuntut Umum melalui Penyidik Pejabat Polisi Negara Republik Indonesia, sesuai dengan ketentuan yang diatur dalam Undang-Undang Hukum Acara Pidana.

translated_text:
Article 99

(1) Certain Civil Servant Officials within the Regional Government are granted special authority as investigators to conduct investigations into criminal acts regulated in this Regional Regulation as referred to in the Criminal Procedure Code.

(2) The investigative authority as referred to in paragraph (1), is as follows: a. receiving, seeking, collecting, and examining information or reports concerning criminal acts of protection of children and women so that such information or reports become more complete and clear;

b. examining, seeking, and collecting information regarding individuals or entities concerning the truth of acts committed in connection with criminal acts of protection of children and women; c. requesting information and evidence from individuals or entities in connection with criminal acts of protection of children and women;

d. examining books, records, and other documents concerning criminal acts of protection of children and women;

JDIH Kota Singkawang

e. conducting searches to obtain evidentiary materials in the form of books, records, and other documents, and conducting seizure of such evidentiary materials;

f. requesting the assistance of experts in the framework of carrying out investigation duties for criminal acts of protection of children and women; g. ordering to stop and/or prohibiting someone from leaving a room or place when an examination is in progress and examining the identity of persons, objects, and/or documents carried; h. photographing persons related to criminal acts of protection of children and women;

i. summoning persons to be heard for their statements and examined as suspects or witnesses;

J. terminating the investigation; and/or

k. taking other actions necessary for the smooth investigation of criminal acts of protection of children and women in accordance with the provisions of Laws and Regulations.

(3) In the event that the investigation meets the elements as referred to in paragraph (1), the Investigator notifies the commencement of the investigation and submits the investigation results to the Public Prosecutor through the Investigator Official of the State Police of the Republic of Indonesia, in accordance with the provisions stipulated in the Criminal Procedure Code.
